<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thyssen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1871</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Thyssen &amp; Co., Thyssen AG</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thyssen was a German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a> and industrial company founded in 1871 by August Thyssen at Mülheim in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruhr">Ruhr</a>. It grew into one of the largest integrated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a>, iron and steel concerns in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, rivalling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krupp">Krupp</a>. Later part of United Steelworks and refounded after 1945, Thyssen merged with Krupp in 1999 to form ThyssenKrupp.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thyssen.jpg" alt="Thyssen" width="320" height="232" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thyssen AG (Founder: August Thyssen) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thyssen_Logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
